### 26.
Consider:

python
name = "Rahul"
Name = "Amit"


Are name and Name treated as the same name in Python? Explain why.
### Answer 
No, name and Name are not treated as the same name.

Python is case-sensitive, so uppercase and lowercase letters are different.

### 27.
What is wrong with using names such as x, y, and z everywhere in a large program? Is using short names always wrong?

### Answer
Using x, y, and z everywhere can make a large program difficult to understand because their purpose is not clear.
Short names are not always wrong. They can be useful when their meaning is obvious, such as i in a loop.

